## Conclusions and limits

The render-node harness works. Firmware-backed GPU initialization reports GPU_ID=308,
chip ID 0x03000620, 128 KiB GMEM. Hardware surfaceless Mesa reports FD306A.
Two executions of the GLES2 RGBA8888 POT nearest-filter test and one NPOT execution
passed. Each test performed four image comparisons and logged four 64x64 PNG readbacks.
All four POT PNG hashes were identical between executions. No new GPU/IOMMU fault or
hangcheck messages appeared after initialization. This demonstrates rendering and completed
readback, not just successful DRM open; fences were not separately instrumented.
This DOES NOT reproduce, resolve, or rule out the reported STK corruption.
No STK trace replay, full conformance suite, native KMS, thermal policy, runtime-PM fix,
kexec, cold-boot repeatability, stock-firmware equivalence, or blob-wrangler extraction is claimed.
Only one PocketBoot RAM boot was tested in this trial. No eMMC filesystem was mounted,
no device partition was written, and no SD card was formatted or prepared.

